{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Moon","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type covers phase angles, illumination, quarter searches, position and velocity, libration, and node crossings."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Phase-Angle","text":"Phase Angle","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The phase angle indicates the Moon’s position in its cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","print(\"Phase angle: \\(angle)°\")","\/\/ 0° = New Moon, 90° = First Quarter, 180° = Full, 270° = Third Quarter"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Phase-Names-and-Emoji","text":"Phase Names and Emoji","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Convert angles to human-readable descriptions:"}]},{"code":["let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","","print(Moon.phaseName(for: angle))  \/\/ \"Waxing Gibbous\"","print(Moon.emoji(for: angle))      \/\/ \"🌔\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The eight phase names:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"New Moon (🌑)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Waxing Crescent (🌒)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"First Quarter (🌓)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Waxing Gibbous (🌔)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Full Moon (🌕)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Waning Gibbous (🌖)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Third Quarter (🌗)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Waning Crescent (🌘)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"anchor":"Illumination","text":"Illumination","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Calculate the fraction of the Moon that’s lit:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let angle = try Moon.phaseAngle(at: .now)","let illumination = Moon.illumination(for: angle)","print(\"Moon is \\(Int(illumination * 100))% illuminated\")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Finding-Quarter-Phases","text":"Finding Quarter Phases","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Search-for-a-Specific-Phase","text":"Search for a Specific Phase","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Next full moon (nil if none occurs within the search window)","if let fullMoon = try Moon.searchPhase(.full, after: .now) {","    print(\"Next full moon: \\(fullMoon)\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Get-the-Next-Quarter","text":"Get the Next Quarter","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let quarter = try Moon.searchQuarter(after: .now)","print(\"\\(quarter.phase.emoji) \\(quarter.phase.name) at \\(quarter.time)\")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"All-Quarters-in-a-Date-Range","text":"All Quarters in a Date Range","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let start = AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 1, day: 1)","let end = AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 2, day: 1)","","let quarters = try Moon.quarters(from: start, to: end)","for quarter in quarters {","    print(\"\\(quarter.phase.emoji) \\(quarter.time)\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Lunar-Position","text":"Lunar Position","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Ecliptic-Coordinates","text":"Ecliptic Coordinates","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let position = try Moon.ecliptic(at: .now)","print(\"Longitude: \\(position.longitude)°\")","print(\"Latitude: \\(position.latitude)°\")","print(\"Distance: \\(position.distance) AU\")"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Ecliptic-Position-and-Velocity","text":"Ecliptic Position and Velocity","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For the Moon’s speed along the ecliptic, ask for the state instead of differencing two positions:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let state = try Moon.eclipticState(at: .now)","print(\"Longitude: \\(state.longitude)°\")","print(\"Rate: \\(state.longitudeRate)°\/day\")  \/\/ About 12 to 15"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The position fields match ","type":"text"},{"code":"Moon.ecliptic(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bit for bit. The rates are a central difference of the lunar series inside the engine, per Terrestrial Time day, accurate to roughly 1e-7 degrees per day. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialPositions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the full rate contract.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Cartesian-State","text":"Cartesian State","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the Moon’s geocentric state vector in equatorial J2000 coordinates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let state = try Moon.geoState(at: .now)","","\/\/ Position in AU","print(\"Distance: \\(state.position.magnitude) AU\")","","\/\/ Velocity in AU\/day","let speed = sqrt(","    state.velocity.x * state.velocity.x +","    state.velocity.y * state.velocity.y +","    state.velocity.z * state.velocity.z",")","print(\"Speed: \\(speed) AU\/day\")"]},{"type":"aside","name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eclipticState(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"geoState(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for velocities. Differencing two positions a short interval apart is noisier and costs two calls."}]}],"style":"tip"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Using-CelestialBody","text":"Using CelestialBody","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Moon is also available as a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialBody","type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let horizon = try CelestialBody.moon.horizon(at: .now, from: observer)","let equatorial = try CelestialBody.moon.equatorial(at: .now)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Libration","anchor":"Libration","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Libration is the Moon’s apparent wobble that lets us see slightly more than 50% of its surface:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let lib = Moon.libration(at: .now)","","\/\/ Sub-Earth point (what's at the center of the visible disc)","print(\"Latitude: \\(lib.subEarthLatitude)°\")","print(\"Longitude: \\(lib.subEarthLongitude)°\")","","\/\/ Distance and apparent size","print(\"Distance: \\(Int(lib.distanceKM)) km\")","print(\"Apparent diameter: \\(lib.apparentDiameter)°\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Interpret libration values:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive latitude: More of the north polar region is visible"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positive longitude: More of the Moon’s east limb is visible"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Lunar Nodes","anchor":"Lunar-Nodes","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The nodes are where the Moon’s orbit crosses the ecliptic plane:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Find next node crossing","let node = try Moon.searchNode(after: .now)","print(\"\\(node.kind.symbol) \\(node.kind.name) at \\(node.time)\")","\/\/ Output: \"☊ Ascending Node at 2025-01-15...\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Node Types","anchor":"Node-Types","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ascending (☊): the Moon crosses from south to north of the ecliptic"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Descending (☋): the Moon crosses from north to south"}]}]}]},{"text":"All Nodes in a Range","anchor":"All-Nodes-in-a-Range","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let nodes = try Moon.nodeCrossings(","    from: AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 1, day: 1),","    to: AstroTime(year: 2025, month: 12, day: 31)",")","for node in nodes {","    print(\"\\(node.kind.symbol) \\(node.time)\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Lunar Apsis","anchor":"Lunar-Apsis","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Find perigee (closest) and apogee (farthest) points:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let apsis = try Moon.searchApsis(after: .now)","print(\"\\(apsis.kind.lunarName): \\(Int(apsis.distanceKM)) km\")","\/\/ Output: \"Perigee: 356,500 km\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"All Apsides in a Range","anchor":"All-Apsides-in-a-Range","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let apsides = try Moon.apsides(","    from: .now,","    to: .now.addingDays(60)",")","for apsis in apsides {","    print(\"\\(apsis.kind.lunarName) at \\(apsis.time)\")","}"]},{"text":"Moonrise and Moonset","anchor":"Moonrise-and-Moonset","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/CelestialBody","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" interface:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)","","if let moonrise = try CelestialBody.moon.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Moonrise: \\(moonrise)\")","}","","if let moonset = try CelestialBody.moon.setTime(after: .now, from: observer) {","    print(\"Moonset: \\(moonset)\")","}"]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Moon Phases","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhases"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/moonphases"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Moon","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhase","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonQuarter","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Libration","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/LunarNode","doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/NodeKind"],"generated":true,"title":"Moon","anchor":"Moon"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Calculate moon phases, quarters, libration, and lunar nodes.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/MoonPhase":{"title":"MoonPhase","url":"\/documentation\/astronomykit\/moonphase","abstract":[{"text":"A phase of the Moon.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MoonPhase"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/MoonPhase","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MoonPhase"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/Moon":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Moon-specific calculations."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"Moon","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Moon","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Moon","kind":"identi